 "caveats": [
  "Coverage: 7 of METR's 26 models have an Epoch training-compute estimate; 3 of those are Confident or Likely, 4 Speculative (within a factor of 30). No model released after GPT-5 (Aug 2025) has one: the labs stopped disclosing, and Epoch's rows read Unknown or Not disclosed.",
  "Epoch's figures are estimates of total training compute, mostly pre-training; how much reinforcement-learning post-training they include varies by row and is often unstated. The horizon gains of 2024-26 came largely from post-training and inference-time reasoning, which these numbers may not price.",
  "Compute and release date rise together across these models, so a fit on compute alone credits compute with whatever time brought (data, methods, post-training), and a fit on both splits the two unstably with this few points (see the chart's note).",
  "Four models (GPT-4 Turbo twice, Claude 3 Opus, GPT-4o) have an Epoch figure only as a benchmark imputation in its notes; it is kept in `mapping` as imputed_flop_not_used and left off the points.",
  "Two points are stand-ins, as METR's own are: davinci-002 for GPT-3 (dated to GPT-3's paper) and gpt-3.5-turbo-instruct dated to text-davinci-002's release; their compute is the model METR says the point stands for.",
  "The METR caveats in metr_horizon.json apply unchanged: automatically scored tasks, a 16-hour ruler, a lower bound at the top, METR no longer updating."
 ],
